WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.990
28 October 312.

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.220
Two Roman armies meet at
a bridge over the Tiber,

3
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.000
just outside Rome.

4
00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.770
Constantine's soldiers carry
a new sign on their shields:

5
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.750
a monogram of Christ.

6
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.070
He wins.

7
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.710
The next year, at Milan, Christians
are granted freedom of worship.

8
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:25.090
Yet he is baptised only on his
deathbed, 25 years after the battle.

9
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:29.040
An emperor puts a Christian
sign on his soldiers' shields.

10
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.220
Was it faith, politics, or both?

11
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.680
In this mission, you'll read two
ancient accounts of the sign,

12
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.920
and compare what each one says.

13
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.640
Then you'll weigh the
evidence for each motive:

14
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:43.870
sincere, political, or mixed.

15
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.710
Your mission: weigh up whether
Constantine acted from faith,

16
00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.320
politics, or both.
